       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d8f3963776d6a44b9e3e1ce67e9a4097?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FNT-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Nigel Thomas",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Aa65de870-9b85-487b-b3e4-8b80c5ab81c2",
      "timeZone": "Europe/London"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The evaluate method exposed in an API would be really useful as Steve pointed out. At York we use the evaluate call to index evaluation results for controlled access to searching and browsing in our interface(s). ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "We have done some work studying the performance issues within XACML evaluation cycle and have found that some performance gains could be had by batching up evaluation calls as well. The PDP implementation from Muradora also support a BatchEvaluate call in addition to evaluate, it would useful expose both methods.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "If performance enhancements could be had by exchanging data in binary format with evaluate call, I would be all for that too! ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
