  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The Muradora codebase included an \"evaluate\" API method which allowed specification of subject, roles, actions, pid and (optional) dsid to determine if the specified action would be permissible in the given context.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The code is present in FeSL eg at org.fcrepo.server.security.xacml.pep.ContextHandlerImpl.evaluate",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This method would be useful for front-end applications so that, for instance, a user interface appropriate to a user's permissions can be presented.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
